(Bug #131: a call with no arguments written directly means its result in
 every position, exactly like a call written with an argument.)

To greeting.
    Return a text, "hello".

To seven.
    Return a number, 7.

To half.
    Return a float, 0.5.

To 'some numbers'.
    Return a list, [1, 2, 3].

Print greeting.
Print seven.
Print half.
Print 'some numbers'.

a text called words is "".
Set words to greeting.
Print words.
a number called count is 0.
Set count to seven.
Print count.
count is seven.
Print count.
a list called scores is [9].
Set scores to 'some numbers'.
Print scores.

Print "say {greeting}, {seven:04}, {half:.2}!".
